  "build_status": "Recorded strict source build of the complete general-stability import closure and all-theorem transitive axiom audit from 19 October 2026. These checks were not rerun for this documentation update. Prior projects retain their recorded independent builds. Shared modules are counted in each standalone project; counts are not numbers of distinct mathematical results.",
  "indexing": "Index translation. In the semi-infinite modules, factors are numbered from zero on the right: a j n corresponds to the paper's hat a_(p-j)(n). The auxiliary index k for next minors has paper order k+1. inverseMinorRatio a p k n corresponds to kappa_(k+1,n+1). Consequently next_minor_at_zero is needed separately for the n=0 determinant identity. cumulative, ratioAt and normalizedTail represent pi, r and chi, respectively. Names containing old proposition numbers are stable code identifiers, not current manuscript numbers. In the stability modules, blockProduct w s N multiplies w(s+1),...,w(s+N); the initial row is zero. In the periodic adjacent-ratio module, w(t)=a(t+1)/b(t) represents manuscript gamma(t+1). The general_stability product API numbers bidiagonal factors from the left. FactorOrderBridge and RelativeFactorOrder prove the exact reversal needed by the legacy inverse-entry API. Row zero is a dummy factor entry. Fixed variations begin at row p-i for zero-based factor i, preserving exactly p(p-1)/2 physical initial entries. Relative maps represent the exact entrywise error divided by its original positive entry.",
