    {
      "label": "stab:lem:weighted-shift",
      "part": "Complete scalar lemma on the Banach space of bounded sequences",
      "hypotheses_and_scope": "Bounded nonnegative weights (thus including the positive weights in the manuscript). The actual continuous linear difference operator I-W includes its initial equation. Bijectivity iff uniform geometric decay, an explicit continuous linear inverse with norm at most 1+C*rho/(1-rho), and equivalence with contraction of one block are proved. Row-sum boundedness iff decay is also proved without an a priori bound on the weights. This does not by itself formalize the PBF multiplication derivative.",
