    {
      "label": "stab:rem:general-radius",
      "part": "Abstract quantitative radius and exact combinatorial estimates; partial coverage of the matrix proposition",
      "hypotheses_and_scope": "A complete real normed variation space, a continuous linear equivalence D with inverse norm bound M, and explicit quadratic/Lipschitz remainder estimates are inputs. Existence and uniqueness in the closed ball, the 3r/4 image bound, the 2M solution Lipschitz bound and positivity at least alpha/2 are proved. The exact C_p majorants are proved for all p>=2, with formal index p=d+2. The two-factor product remainder is verified in an arbitrary normed ring. The exact matrix-specific quantitative-radius application remains partial: the general band-matrix realization of these numerical remainder bounds is not formalized. General analytic factorization criteria are covered separately below.",
